guide forever/50-60/mount-hyjal
title Mount Hyjal
levels 56-58 Alliance
levels 56-58 Horde
zone Mount Hyjal
coords live
why About 100 quests in Forever's new endgame zone, 57 to 59, then on to Silithus.
keywords mount hyjal, hyjal, tainted foothills, felblood scar, ketharas, moonglade, barkskin burrow, elderwild, mourning's rest, cradle of tranquility, shrine of aviana, dae'gun, summit of eternity, nordrassil
next forever/horde/50-60/06-silithus
next forever/alliance/50-60/06-silithus

# Mount Hyjal for both factions (2026-11-12; in both routes since 0.4.3). Hand-written. Quests, givers, enders,
# levels and objectives come from Forever's quest data (QuestieDB 1.0.16 and EG Link, as merged into data/forever);
# the order, the objective spots and the chain links the data lacks come from players' recordings of the zone: the
# first Alliance player (levels 57 to 60), then Alliance players who followed this guide and Horde players who quested
# through the zone (levels 55 to 60, 2026-11). The Horde steps (Thark Gorax, the Western Post, Elderwild's Zet'gan,
# Ortak Lomgok and Kal'tinzan, Faustron's Moonglade flight path, Thisalee's hand-in) follow the Horde recordings.
# On both routes it comes before the faction's Silithus guide (50-60/06), at about 56 (Alliance) and 56.3 (Horde) by
# the level model. Alliance: after the Western & Eastern Plaguelands guide (50-60/04, which ends in Menethil Harbor on
# the boat to Theramore); Horde: after the Eastern Plaguelands guide (50-60/05, which ends at Everlook in Winterspring).
# Both fly to Everlook, ride in through Darkwhisper Gorge and leave from the Summit of Eternity by the flight to
# Everlook; the Silithus guides pick up from there (the Alliance's with Everlook's errands, the Horde's with the flight
# from Everlook to Gadgetzan).
# Order: the way in from Everlook through Darkwhisper Gorge (binding the Hearthstone there), Ketharas the hermit
# and his first errands by the road, the Tainted Foothills in one loop (Kaylaena's workshop, the ancients' outpost
# and its flight path, the fields south and the shrub field), Ketharas again, the outpost, Felblood Scar (the
# Curious Crow and Felflick), Velician, then Ketharas's errand to Moonglade (by Bluebell's flight, or through Everlook
# where the Hearthstone is bound) with the parts order from Everlook on the way back.
# Offered only after another quest is handed in (the recordings): Violence Into
# Verdure after Seeds for a New Season, The Bounty of Nature after Hope for Hatchlings, Rites of Respect after The
# Bounty of Nature, Ancient Allies after Rites of Respect; Bark Bite after Leaves to Ligatures; Fine Feathered
# Friend and The Dying Ancients after Bark Bite; Felflick's chain one quest at a time; A Revenge Now Bitter after
# Amalgamated Marrow; A Prolific Source and Prickly Pinecones after Notation, Notation, Notation; The Experimental
# Method after A Prolific Source; The Western Post after The Experimental Method; An Oldstone But An Old Friend
# after The Dying God; Rubble Rummage after Crate Expectations; The Capricious Corvid and Taking to New Heights
# after The Pact.
# Behind a group choice: Celastrus the Bitter (91923), The Dying Ancients (92959) and Amalgamated Marrow (96255):
# Celastrus, Sunderbark and the Awakened Fel Ash Slime are elites (levels 57, 56 and 58), and A Revenge Now Bitter
# (96322) comes only after Amalgamated Marrow. The slime rose the moment A Fitting End was handed in at the bone
# pile in the recording, before Amalgamated Marrow was taken, so that step warns everyone. Ghansurok (elite 61)
# prowls around Kaylaena's workshop (the data's spawns and the recording's sightings).
# Not in the first recording, from the quest data alone: Venom Maws (96833) and One Person's Trash (94479).
# The ride in (0.4.3): Frostmaul Giants and Preservers (elite, 59-60) stand on both sides of the road through
# Frostwhisper Gorge, and Hederine Slayers, Initiates and Manastalkers (elite, 57-58) line Darkwhisper Gorge from its
# mouth (about 59.5,75) to the zone line, with Lady Hederine (61) on its east side. Thirteen recorded crossings took
# the same line, which the step's waypoints follow; nobody killed one of the elites, and four of the six Alliance
# players who followed this guide died on the way in (levels 55.5 to 58.4).
# Kits and Cats (93615): each of Shalla'kal's kittens counts as you walk up to her, so each is a `talk` goal (93615.1-3).

step Into Mount Hyjal
  when !zone "Mount Hyjal"
  tip New in Forever: this guide follows what players did on Mount Hyjal. If a step is wrong, tell us on Polestar's Discord or GitHub and name the step.
  tip Mount Hyjal lies south of Winterspring. Fly to Everlook (from Theramore on the Alliance route; the Horde route already ends there), bind your Hearthstone at the inn (partway through this guide Ketharas sends you to Moonglade, and the way there starts in Everlook), then ride south down the road through Frostwhisper Gorge and on through Darkwhisper Gorge, which leads up into Mount Hyjal.
  tip Careful: elites stand along the whole way in. Frostmaul Giants and Preservers (59-60) flank the road through Frostwhisper Gorge, and Hederine Slayers, Initiates and Manastalkers (57-58) line Darkwhisper Gorge from its mouth to the zone line, with Lady Hederine (61) on its east side. Follow the arrows' line at full speed, never stop or fight on the way, and don't turn off it.
  fly "Everlook"
  zone Winterspring
  sethome "Everlook" npc 11118          -- Innkeeper Vizzie
  goto 62.3,67.0 "The road through Frostwhisper Gorge"
  goto 60.3,73.0 "The mouth of Darkwhisper Gorge"
  goto 59.2,76.5
  goto 61.2,79.5
  goto 61.1,81.5
  goto 58.3,82.2 "Turn west here"
  goto 56.6,80.7
  goto 55.6,83.0
  goto 53.5,84.6
  goto 50.5,83.2 "Into Mount Hyjal"
  zone Mount Hyjal
  enter "Mount Hyjal" @85.5,73.2

step The road in
  tip Quintus Wainworth (Alliance) and Thark Gorax (Horde) wait together by the road a little inside the zone.
  accept 96833 only Alliance            -- Venom Maws: for Ketharas, the hermit
  accept 96830 only Horde               -- Farsight Guided: for Ortak Lomgok in Elderwild, later in this guide; keep it

step Loose Cog
  tip The cog lies by the path south-west of the camp, on your way to Ketharas.
  accept 94479                          -- One Person's Trash

step Ketharas
  tip Ketharas, the hermit, lives at the Hermit's Abode a little further south-west. He takes the cog too.
  turnin 96833 only Alliance
  turnin 94479
  accept 95568                          -- Seeds for a New Season
  accept 95569                          -- Hope for Hatchlings
  accept 96796                          -- Woods Workshop: for Kaylaena, on the way

step Seeds and owl eggs
  tip The seeds and the owl eggs lie on the slopes between the Hermit's Abode and the road you came in on: search north-east up towards Quintus and Thark.
  loop
  goto 74.0,79.0
  goto 77.5,75.5
  goto 79.0,70.5
  goto 81.5,68.0
  collect 260176 x10 quest 95568.1      -- Untainted Seed
  collect 269920 x12 quest 95569.1      -- Hyjal Owl Egg

step Ketharas
  turnin 95568
  turnin 95569
  accept 93747                          -- Violence Into Verdure
  accept 93759                          -- The Bounty of Nature

step Kaylaena's workshop
  tip North-west over the shrub field to Kaylaena Springwhisper's workshop on the slope above it. Celastrus the Bitter, an elite (level 57), patrols the field, and Sunderbark, an elite ancient (level 56), stands in its middle: give both room. Ghansurok, an elite chimaera (level 61), prowls around the workshop itself: see where he is before you ride up to Kaylaena.
  turnin 96796                          -- Kaylaena Springwhisper
  accept 92594                          -- Kindling, Kinda
  accept 92008                          -- Premiere Parts: for Nami in Everlook; you go there from Moonglade at the end of this guide

step The ancients' outpost
  tip South down the west side of the shrub field to the ancients' outpost: kill the Tainted Shrubbery you pass for Kaylaena. Bluebell, the flight mistress, waits by the outpost; Hyacinth and Thylaen stand with the ancient Fraxinus.
  getfp "Tainted Foothills"             -- Bluebell
  accept 91754                          -- Hyacinth: Rub Some Dirt In It
  accept 91755                          -- Leaves to Ligatures

step Celastrus the Bitter
  when group 91923
  tip Celastrus the Bitter is elite (level 57) and patrols the shrub field: grouping up is advised.
  accept 91923                          -- Thylaen

step Soil and venison
  tip The untainted soil lies in the fields south and east of the outpost; Hyjal Stags graze there too, and their venison is for Ketharas's stew.
  tip Careful: Sunderbark (56), an elite treant, walks the fields to the south-east around 60,78: give him room.
  loop
  goto 56.5,83.5
  goto 57.2,89.5
  goto 61.6,83.3
  goto 64.2,83.3
  collect 247889 x6 quest 91754.1       -- Untainted Soil
  collect 251641 x2 quest 93759.1       -- Hyjal Venison Cut

step The ruined catapult and flying machine
  tip Two of the wrecks Ketharas named lie at the east end of the fields: use the Bag of Enchanted Seeds beside each.
  use 269944 quest 93747.2 @62.9,82.9   -- Bag of Enchanted Seeds: the Ruined Catapult
  use 269944 quest 93747.3 @66.1,83.5   -- Bag of Enchanted Seeds: the Ruined Flying Machine

step The shrub field
  tip North into the shrub field: the Tainted Shrubbery drop the leaves, and the Scarlet Dart Tubers grow in the open ground, most of them in the field's western half. The ruined ballista stands at the field's north-eastern edge: use the Bag of Enchanted Seeds to plant the last seed there. Keep clear of Celastrus the Bitter and Sunderbark, the field's elites.
  kill 248395 x15 quest 92594.1         -- Tainted Shrubbery
  collect 247892 x12 quest 91755.1      -- Verdant Leaves
  collect 267289 x6 quest 93759.2 @59.5,73.5  -- Scarlet Dart Tuber
  use 269944 quest 93747.1 @70.4,70.7   -- Bag of Enchanted Seeds: the Ruined Ballista

step Celastrus
  when group 91923
  tip Celastrus the Bitter is elite: grouping up is advised. He walks the shrub field.
  collect 282028 quest 91923.1          -- Broken Frond of Celastrus

step Ketharas
  tip South-east back to the Hermit's Abode.
  turnin 93747
  turnin 93759
  accept 95611                          -- Rites of Respect

step Ketharas's shrine
  tip The shrine is a pair of standing stones west of the Hermit's Abode, on the way back to the outpost: bury the remains there.
  complete 95611 @66.7,84.3

step Ketharas
  turnin 95611
  accept 90487                          -- Ancient Allies

step The ancients' outpost
  tip West to the outpost.
  turnin 90487                          -- Fraxinus
  turnin 91754                          -- Hyacinth
  turnin 91755
  accept 91770                          -- Bark Bite
  complete 91770 @53.4,84.3             -- put the poultice on Fraxinus
  turnin 91770
  accept 95766                          -- Fine Feathered Friend

step Thylaen
  when onquest 91923
  turnin 91923

step The Dying Ancients
  when group 92959
  tip Sunderbark is an elite corrupted ancient (level 56) in the middle of the shrub field, back east: grouping up is advised.
  accept 92959                          -- Fraxinus

step Sunderbark
  when group 92959
  tip Sunderbark is elite: grouping up is advised.
  kill 248709                           -- Sunderbark
  complete 92959 @63.1,73.8             -- plant the seed in his remains

step Fraxinus
  when onquest 92959
  turnin 92959

step The Curious Crow
  tip West of the outpost to Felblood Scar: the Curious Crow perches at its southern end.
  turnin 95766                          -- Curious Crow
  accept 95317                          -- Notation, Notation, Notation
  accept 95320                          -- A Curious Question

step Felflick
  tip North to Felflick, a demon caged in the middle of the scar. He stood at the spot marked here every time he was met in the recording, south of where the quest data puts him.
  turnin 95320 @49.3,77.1               -- Felflick
  accept 95318 @49.3,77.1               -- Taste of Ash

step The Ashen camp
  tip The Ashen Acolytes hold the camp at the north of the scar. Not every Acolyte carries notes: keep killing them after the twelve kills until you have all twelve notes.
  tip Careful: Awakened Fel Ash Slimes (58, elite) ooze about the scar: pull the Acolytes away from them.
  kill 260422 x12 quest 95318.1         -- Ashen Acolyte
  collect 274396 x12 quest 95317.1      -- Fel Ash Experimentation Notes

step Felflick
  turnin 95318 @49.3,77.1
  accept 95319 @49.3,77.1               -- Crystalline Collection

step Fel-slime crystals
  tip The crystals grow in the scar west and south of Felflick. The pristine one turned up at the scar's southern end, close to the Curious Crow, at the spot marked.
  collect 274412 x8 quest 95319.1 @46.9,74.4  -- Fel-Slime Crystal
  collect 268990 quest 95319.2 @48.1,82.7  -- Pristine Fel-Slime Crystal

step The Curious Crow
  tip The Crow is just south of the pristine crystal.
  turnin 95317
  accept 95380                          -- A Prolific Source
  accept 96262                          -- Prickly Pinecones

step Slime ooze as you go
  along until crow-ooze
  background
  tip The Noxious Slimes crawl all over the scar's southern half, and not every one leaves ooze: kill the ones you pass from here on.
  tip Careful: Awakened Fel Ash Slimes (elites, 58) ooze among the slimes: leave them be.
  collect 273008 x8 quest 95380.1       -- Fel-Slime Ooze

step Felflick
  turnin 95319 @49.3,77.1
  accept 95378 @49.3,77.1               -- The Hydra's Head
  accept 95379 @49.3,77.1               -- A Revenge So Sweet

step The warlocks
  tip The three warlocks and Brashann Grimdark are in and around the Ashen camp at the north of the scar.
  tip Careful: Awakened Fel Ash Slimes (58, elite) ooze about the scar: keep clear of them.
  collect 273291 quest 95378.1          -- Bones of Tyaeha Darkoath
  collect 273292 quest 95378.2          -- Bones of Dazka Shadowsleep
  collect 273290 quest 95378.3          -- Bones of Frezzlie Popwhiz
  kill 260440 quest 95379.1             -- Brashann Grimdark

step Felflick
  turnin 95378 @49.3,77.1
  turnin 95379 @49.3,77.1
  accept 96435 @49.3,77.1               -- A Fitting End

step The bone pile
  tip West to the bone pile by the slime pools: throw the warlocks' bones on it, then hand the quest in at the pile itself. Handing it in wakes the Awakened Fel Ash Slime, an elite (level 58) that hits hard: unless you are grouped for it, hand in and ride clear at once.
  complete 96435 @40.8,80.3
  turnin 96435                          -- Bone Pile

step Amalgamated Marrow
  when group 96255
  tip The bone pile wakes the Awakened Fel Ash Slime, an elite (level 58) that hits hard: grouping up is advised.
  accept 96255                          -- Bone Pile
  kill 264306 quest 96255.1             -- Awakened Fel Ash Slime

step Prickly pinecones
  tip The pinecones lie under the healthy trees just south of the bone pile, on the scar's south-western rim, and a few east of the Crow.
  collect 273304 x10 quest 96262.1 @40.0,83.5  -- Prickly Pinecone

step Felflick
  when onquest 96255
  turnin 96255 @49.3,77.1
  accept 96322 @49.3,77.1               -- A Revenge Now Bitter
  complete 96322 @49.3,77.2             -- Felflick: decide his fate

step Finish the slime ooze
  when !has 273008 x8
  tip The slimes are thickest in the scar's south-western corner.
  collect 273008 x8 quest 95380.1 @44.5,83.5  -- Fel-Slime Ooze

step The Curious Crow
  label crow-ooze
  turnin 95380
  turnin 96262
  accept 95316                          -- The Experimental Method

step The Curious Crow
  when onquest 96322
  turnin 96322

step The Ashen workstations
  tip Four workstations stand in the Ashen camp: throw a pinecone at each, from the south up.
  goto 42.5,73.1 "Slime Workstation"
  goto 44.3,68.3 "Alchemy Workstation"
  goto 46.6,68.0 "Disease Workstation"
  goto 49.6,69.6 "Vessel Workstation"
  complete 95316

step The Curious Crow
  turnin 95316
  accept 91881 only Alliance            -- The Western Post: for Sefira Everbright in Elderwild, later in this guide; keep it
  accept 94782 only Horde               -- The Western Post: for Zet'gan in Elderwild, later in this guide; keep it

step Velician
  tip West across the slope from the scar: Velician waits alone.
  accept 96321                          -- The Dying God

step The Curious Crow
  turnin 96321
  accept 96131                          -- An Oldstone But An Old Friend

step Ketharas
  tip East across the foothills to the Hermit's Abode.
  turnin 96131
  accept 92612                          -- Aid from Moonglade

step Fly to Moonglade
  when zone "Mount Hyjal"
  tip Back west to Bluebell at the ancients' outpost and fly to Moonglade. Druids: Teleport: Moonglade is quicker. (No flight path to Moonglade yet? The road in is Timbermaw Hold's tunnel, from Winterspring or Felwood.)
  goto 55.1,82.6 "Bluebell, the flight mistress"
  fly "Moonglade"

step Fly to Moonglade
  when zone "Winterspring"
  tip Fly to Moonglade from Everlook's flight master. No flight path to Moonglade yet? The way in is the tunnel through Timbermaw Hold, at the western end of Winterspring.
  fly "Moonglade"
  zone Moonglade

step Dendrite Starblaze
  tip North into Nighthaven: Dendrite Starblaze stands in the north-east of the village, upstairs in his building: go up inside, the arrow cannot tell the floors apart.
  turnin 92612
  accept 96209                          -- The Ancient, Orokai

step Orokai
  tip South-west to Orokai, the ancient. Talk to him again when you are ready and watch what he shows you.
  turnin 96209
  accept 95006                          -- Stolen Power
  complete 95006                        -- Orokai: ready to watch

step Dendrite Starblaze
  tip Dendrite stands upstairs in his building: go up inside, the arrow cannot tell the floors apart.
  turnin 95006
  accept 93773                          -- The Pact: for Ketharas

step Rabine Saturna
  only Alliance
  when onquest 6762
  zone Moonglade
  tip Rabine Saturna's house stands in Nighthaven, a short walk from Dendrite: hand her the letter from Darnassus on the way to the flight master.
  turnin 6762                           -- Rabine Saturna
  accept 1124                           -- For Layo Starstrike in Silithus, on the next guide: keep it

step Fly to Everlook
  tip South to Moonglade's flight master (the Alliance's at the southern end of the valley, the Horde's at its south-western end) and fly to Everlook for Kaylaena's parts order.
  getfp "Moonglade" npc 10897 only Alliance  -- Sindrayl
  getfp "Moonglade" npc 12740 only Horde  -- Faustron
  fly "Everlook"
  zone Winterspring

step Nami
  tip Nami stands between Everlook's two flight masters. Her crate holds fragile cells that fizzle out in time and when knocked about: fly straight back to the Tainted Foothills and take it to Kaylaena without detours or fights (about four minutes in the recording). If it fizzles out anyway, Nami fills it again.
  turnin 92008                          -- Nami
  accept 92009                          -- Crate Expectations

step Fly to the Tainted Foothills
  fly "Tainted Foothills"
  zone Mount Hyjal

step Kaylaena's workshop
  tip North from Bluebell to the workshop, crate first. Watch for Ghansurok, the elite chimaera (level 61) that prowls around the workshop.
  complete 92009                        -- deliver the crate before it fizzles
  turnin 92009                          -- Kaylaena Springwhisper
  turnin 92594
  accept 92011                          -- Rubble Rummage: in Dae'gun, later in this guide; keep it

step Ketharas
  tip South-east to the Hermit's Abode.
  turnin 93773
  accept 96930                          -- The Capricious Corvid: for the Curious Crow, later in this guide
  accept 92171                          -- Taking to New Heights: for Skylord Omnuron, later in this guide

# Mount Hyjal part 2 of 3, for both factions (2026-11-12). Hand-written.
# Sources as in part 1: Forever's quest data for quests, givers, enders and objectives; players' recordings for the
# order, the spots and the chain links the data lacks. The Horde's Elderwild steps follow the Horde players'
# recordings (2026-11): the Western Post and Farsight Guided handed in, then Zet'gan's quests, Kal'tinzan's flags and
# Ortak's herbs taken, Head Scratcher offered once Feathers in Flight is handed in, Ortak's poultice errand to Maruke
# and Enho after the herbs.
# Order: the Curious Crow, Malorne's Retreat (Alliance), Barkskin Burrow (Brerufa's Den Guardians, then Osi's
# berries, then the elders) with the Deadwood camps around it, Elderwild (the Alliance and Horde outposts stand
# side by side) with Mourning's Rest and the overlook west of it, then east into the Cradle of Tranquility: the
# wild gods' errands, Johun's camp (Alliance) and back west to Marrosis and Shalla'kal.
# Quest log: since the 2026-11-20 route rounds a character arrives with only a few quests carried from the 50-60 guides
# (flow audit, Alliance route: 2 or 3) and the guide's own log peaks at about 17 of the game's 40.
# The veteran's Anywhere But Here is taken after Mourning's Rest, on the way west to the overlook, and the
# breadcrumbs for part 3 (A Clever Creature, Trail Assist) wait for part 3's way through the Cradle.
# Offered only after another quest is handed in (the recording; one player, so leads to confirm): Heading Up the
# Mountain after The Capricious Corvid; Fenwick's quests one at a time; Of Friend and Fur after Balance Through
# Strength (Brerufa's window held nothing else before that hand-in, which also lifted Barkskin standing from
# Hostile to Unfriendly); Sweetpaw Jam after Of Friend and Fur; Meet the Elders after Sweetpaw Jam; Deal Dread to
# Deadwood after Meet the Elders (Barkbound Blessings and Windswept Wards were first offered then too, so they are
# taken there); More Work? and To the Summit of Eternity after Sefira's three quests;
# More of the Same, then Belle's Ring, then the second Belle's Ring after More Work?; Battle Recall after Anywhere
# But Here; Jereman's three errands after Heading Up the Mountain; Fox Hole after Area Denial Skunks; Resupply after
# Fox Hole; Stolen Life and Bone Sweet Bone after The Balance of Life and Death; Prey and Predator after Violent
# Venison; Trail Assist after Sacred Refreshment.
# Balance Through Strength came to the recorded player as a party share: that Brerufa offers it at Hostile
# standing is not recorded yet.
# Left out on purpose:
# - Barkskin Beginnings (94504): it asks for Neutral with Barkskin Burrow, which this route doesn't reach.
# - Beads for Brerufa (93925): a repeatable hand-in for reputation.
# - Wake Memories (93510) and Lifted by Legacy (92101), after Battle Recall: they send you to Redridge and to
#   Thousand Needles, and the veteran's last errands (Praise 93551, Ends Meet 93567, Soldier's Solace 96558 with
#   an elite spirit, Last Wishes 96561) come back to Mount Hyjal.
# - Ewe Wandered Off (96674): six sheep led back to Mirt one at a time, for little experience (the recorded
#   player dropped it once and took six minutes over it later).
# - The Horde's crafting deliveries (90854, 92433, 95769, 97119).
# - Open Season (91696) and Barkskin Breakout (91698): not recorded, and the data has no hand-in for the first.
# - The Horde's Sawyer errands (97001, 97006, 97007): the data has no giver or hand-in for them.
# Horde (0.4.3): Head Scratcher (92446) is a group choice: he is a level 60 elite in our data (eight Horde players in
# the recordings handed his claws in at 57-58). Kal'tinzan's flags (91794) come from Dae'gun in part 3 and go back to
# Elderwild on a Horde-only ride at the end, with Tribal Colors (96998).
# Final Death (92591, 92592): its Scourge Reanimator is 59-60, so the bone pile is burnt alone only from level 58, else
# as a group choice. The Alliance burns it on the first pass through Mourning's Rest when it is 58 there; the Horde,
# about 0.7 level lower (level model: 57.9 against 58.6), and any Alliance player under 58 then, on the guide's second
# pass (Marrosis' bones), with the hand-in on the ride back to Elderwild at the end. To the Summit of Eternity (91688,
# 95248) is offered only once Final Death is handed in, so it is taken wherever that happens. Final Death is taken
# alone at Elderwild only from 57.6 (Alliance) and 57.85 (Horde): the Horde's second pass comes only about 0.1 level
# after Elderwild (level model 2026-11-20: about 57.25 at Elderwild, 57.34 at the second pass), so a Horde character accepts
# it alone only when it reaches the bone pile at 58; under that it is a group choice. A character still under 58
# after the second pass gets an abandon step, as no later visit comes back for it.
# To the Summit of Eternity's accept steps read `when turnedin` Final Death: accept after Final Death.

step The Curious Crow
  when onquest 96930
  tip West across the foothills, past the ancients' outpost, to the Curious Crow at the southern end of Felblood Scar.
  turnin 96930                          -- Curious Crow
  accept 96931                          -- Heading Up the Mountain: for the Cradle of Tranquility, later in this guide

step Malorne's Retreat
  only Alliance
  tip West along the southern slopes to Malorne's Retreat: Fenwick Togglespring, a gnome test pilot, hangs tangled up in a tree. A sturdy branch lies just south of him.
  accept 92702                          -- Branch Out
  collect 274617 quest 92702.1 @24.9,77.5  -- Sturdy Tree Branch
  turnin 92702
  accept 92064                          -- Tree Free
  kill 254501 quest 92064.1             -- Tree Branch, above Fenwick's head
  turnin 92064
  accept 96559                          -- Supply Drop

step Fenwick's survival pack
  only Alliance
  tip His pack fell just north of the tree. Open it, then wait half a minute while its safety lock discharges before you open it again.
  turnin 96559                          -- Personal Survival Pack
  accept 93383                          -- Contents Under Pressure
  turnin 93383

step Brerufa
  tip North-west to Barkskin Burrow, the furbolgs' den in the hillside: Brerufa waits just north of its mouth. The Barkskin furbolgs show as hostile until your standing with them improves, but none of them attacked in the recording: the Deadwood furbolgs in the camps around are the ones to fight. Brerufa offers more only once this first quest is handed in.
