# Mount Hyjal part 3 of 3, for both factions (2026-11-12; the Horde's steps since 0.4.3). Hand-written.
# The Horde's Dae'gun quests (Kal'tinzan's flag and heraldry, the Troll Remains that start Tribal Colors) and the
# ride back to Elderwild for them follow the Horde players' recordings (2026-11): most took the flags and the remains
# in Dae'gun and handed both in at Elderwild after the Summit.
# Sources as in parts 1 and 2: Forever's quest data for quests, givers, enders and objectives; players' recordings
# for the order, the spots and the chain links the data lacks.
# Order: the Shrine of Aviana and its harpies, back south-west past the Deadwood camps to Barkskin Burrow for its
# three hand-ins, north-east through the Cradle (Galvinquam's and Jereman's breadcrumbs taken on the way) to Johun
# (Alliance) and Dae'gun (Maerion and Renalard first, then the demon camps west to east and back), the Summit of Eternity
# (flight path, inn), a flight down for Kaylaena and Ketharas, then the Summit's Blackthorne camps in one sweep, and
# out by Everlook.
# Quest log: since the 2026-11-20 route rounds a character arrives with only a few quests carried from the 50-60 guides
# (flow audit, Alliance route: 2 or 3) and the guide's own log peaks at about 17 of the game's 40.
# The breadcrumbs for Dae'gun and the Summit (A Clever Creature, Trail Assist) are taken on this part's way
# through the Cradle rather than at the end of part 2, and Fetid Corruption is handed in before the Shrine's three
# quests are taken.
# Offered only after another quest is handed in (the recording; one player, so leads to confirm): A Bit of the
# Sky after Taking to New Heights; Avalanche of Corruption after Resupply; Drawing Down the Malevolent after
# Siphoned Ephemeral Essence; As the Crow Flies after Drawing Down the Malevolent; Ashes of the Legion Ascent and
# To Outfox a Demon after A Clever Creature; Siegecraft after Rubble Rummage; The Staff of the Mountain after
# Stolen Life, Ashes of the Legion Ascent and A Bit of the Sky; Paying Back the Pact after The Staff of the
# Mountain.
# Not checked to the end in the recording (taken, not finished, or not taken): the Summit's Blackthorne quests
# (Cult Closure, Twisted Tools, A Thorn in the Paw, Paying Back the Pact) and Cleansing Winds.
# Maerion's Misery: 13 players' recordings (2026-11) took it from Maerion at 63.2,25.8 with no earlier quest, 4 of
# them while Siphoned Ephemeral Essence was still open; 10 handed it in, most after 15-32 Defiling Hound kills. So
# it is taken before the Dae'gun sweep, its spikes come with the essence, and the last ones by Maerion at the
# hand-in. The Shrine's Spear of the Skylord,
# Highfeather Helper and Tarnished Treasures were offered before Taking to New Heights and Past Wing and Claw were
# handed in (the windows in the recording): the breadcrumbs do not gate them.
# Left out on purpose:
# - Yashiro's Windwalk (96983): its Doomguard Xarkul is an elite (level 61); the recorded player dropped it.
# - Gathering Storm (96494) and A Shaw Deal (96529): the first sends you to the Summit's far end and back to
#   Johun, the second to Stormwind.
# - Blind Vengeance (97010), the Summit's level 60 chain after Paying Back the Pact (Ve'han's Fall 92833 with an
#   elite, Summit Sentries 93127, A Thorny Solution 93547, Challenger of the Gods 93521, Work Well Done 93848,
#   Return to Jereman 99670), Marn's and Thisalee's Well of Eternity quests (92016, 96301, 96302, 96303),
#   Blackthorne Blackout (93422, an elite courier), Drum Up Trouble (92329) and Bait the Beast (93444, both with
#   Ghansurok, an elite chimaera): not recorded yet.
# - The Horde's Wrap Return (96999) is optional: Tai'tasi takes it in Sen'jin Village, Durotar, off this route.
# Drawing Down the Malevolent (96003): Bethra'zel and Mazzogore are level 60 elites until Elaena's eye drains them;
# drained, recorded players killed each of them.

